<section class="home-section prose">
  <h2>Streamlined CSS processor</h2>
  <p>Assemble <code>@import</code>s (including mid-file), optionally lint, and minify. One command from source CSS to output.</p>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">npx argot styles/input.css dist/output.css</code></pre>
  <p class="note">Example shape—flags and package name follow the shipped CLI. Details in <a href="{{ '/docs/processor/' | url }}">processor docs</a>.</p>
  <div class="shell-placeholder">Homepage processor demo polish comes later.</div>
</section>

<section class="home-section prose">
  <h2>Scaffolding for new projects</h2>
  <p><code>argot scaffold</code> drops a layered CSS tree much like this site’s <code>website/styles/</code>: entrypoint, reset, base, primitives, semantics, layout, modules. After write, those files are ordinary project source—edit and run with.</p>
  <p><a href="{{ '/docs/scaffold/' | url }}">Scaffold docs</a> · <a href="{{ '/approach/' | url }}">Why this shape (Mindset)</a></p>
  <div class="shell-placeholder">Short file-tree illustration later.</div>
</section>

